voynich-transliterations: license

Dataset: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

  VCAT's comparison in the variant tables (locus_variants: agreement,
  distinct_readings, majority_baseline; word_alignments: the alignments,
  matches and word_agreement) is CC-BY-4.0. Every row of the per-source
  configurations is the text of one transliteration of the Voynich Manuscript
  (Beinecke MS 408, Yale University), with its page and locus ids, as
  voynich.nu publishes it; voynich.nu makes these transliterations available
  under CC0 (CC0-1.0), and those fields stay CC0 wherever they are reused. The
  statement and where it was read are recorded in data_sources/sources.yaml
  and docs/SOURCES_LICENSE.md of the repository.

  Please cite the transliterators named in the dataset card in published work.

Code that builds the data: MIT License
  https://github.com/noah-chelednik/voynich-data/blob/main/LICENSE

The manuscript itself is in the public domain.
